I need to write a Java class with a method that checks if a string is a valid PIN.

Approach:
- Check if string length is 4 or 6
- Check if all characters are digits
- Can use regex: `\\d{4}|\\d{6}` or `^[0-9]{4}$|^[0-9]{6}$` or simply `\\d{4}|\\d{6}` with matches()
- Or check length and use Character.isDigit() for each char

Simplest solution:
```java
public class PinValidator {
    public static boolean validatePin(String pin) {
        return pin != null && pin.matches("\\d{4}|\\d{6}");
    }
}
```

Or without regex:
```java
public class PinValidator {
    public static boolean validatePin(String pin) {
        if (pin == null) return false;
        int len = pin.length();
        if (len != 4 && len != 6) return false;
        for (char c : pin.toCharArray()) {
            if (!Character.isDigit(c)) return false;
        }
        return true;
    }
}
```

